is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: dns_server
diagnosis_text:
Affected component: The DNS service (BIND/named) on dns_server. Its resolver policy is misconfigured.

Mechanism: Host host_1_1_1_1 uses 10.200.0.2 as its only DNS server (resolv.conf shows nameserver 10.200.0.2). Internal names in the “local” zone (e.g., web0.local) resolve quickly and consistently because the server is authoritative for that zone. However, when pages or “other portals” reference external domains (fonts, CDNs, analytics, etc.), lookups are sent to the same DNS and are refused. Applications then wait for DNS timeouts or rely on cached entries, making page loads seem to hang intermittently and then work again when caches are warm.

Localization: dns_server (10.200.0.2), BIND configuration. Evidenc
